WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:11.690
96. Alpacas. If you're ever traveling in South America, you might see something that

2
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:17.090
looks like a moving mass of fluff darting up a slope. Don't be startled, it's just

3
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:23.150
an alpaca. Alpacas have been domesticated for thousands of years. Humans value them

4
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:29.050
for their soft wool, which the Incas called the fiber of the gods. Alpaca wool can be

5
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:33.990
turned into soft, warm fabrics that would have been very useful to people living at

6
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:39.550
high altitudes in the Andes Mountains. Alpacas are still herded in the foothills of the

7
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:46.770
Andes Mountains. Most alpacas live in Peru, Bolivia, and Chile. They eat hay and grass,

8
00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.030
but they'll try to eat anything. Within the herds, they live in family groups dominated

9
00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.510
by one male, plus females and babies. They are social animals and interact with each

10
00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:03.110
other frequently. They make different sounds to show anger, fear, and happiness, or to

11
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:09.270
warn other alpacas of enemies. They will fight to defend their families. When they fight,

12
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:15.730
they use their front feet, and they spit. Alpacas are part of the Camelide family, which

13
00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:22.970
includes camels and llamas, among other animals. Alpacas look very similar to small llamas.

14
00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:28.690
They are usually about 100-200 pounds and 3 feet high at the shoulder. That's shorter

15
00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:34.450
than most human beings. They are different shades of white, black, brown, or gray. They

16
00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:40.530
may be solid or have spots of different colors. Their thick wool can make them look chubby,

17
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.750
but when shorn, you can see that they are thin and long-legged. They have large features.

18
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:51.050
They can often look like they are making kissing faces under their big eyes. These interesting

19
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:55.930
and unique animals have been part of human culture for thousands of years, and we're

20
00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:58.330
still using them in the same ways today.
